# Grandfathered duplicate migration version prefixes (P1042).
#
# Read by scripts/lib/check-duplicate-migration-versions.sh, called from
# scripts/migrate.sh (apply time, whole tree) and scripts/pre-commit-checks.sh
# (authoring time, staged files only).
#
# Two migration files sharing a version prefix normally ABORT the run, because
# schema_migrations is keyed on the prefix alone: only one of them can ever be
# recorded, and the other is skipped forever while its SQL never runs.
#
# An entry here asserts something specific and checkable: BOTH files of that pair
# already applied in EVERY environment, so renumbering one would make an
# already-applied migration pending again and re-run it — the more dangerous option.
#
# Do NOT add an entry to silence a collision that has not fully applied everywhere.
# That is the P1042 defect itself, not a grandfathered case. Each entry must name how
# "both halves applied" was verified — a query for an object each half creates, run
# against each environment. The ledger cannot answer this: it cannot distinguish the
# two files, which is the entire bug.

